  Cinestill 800 = Moody, cinematic analog photograph, shot on 35mm film stock Cinestill 800T with a vintage SLR camera. Natural, available light only – soft, diffused lighting conditions creating gentle shadows and a dreamy atmosphere. Authentic film grain visible throughout, slight halation around bright light sources, subtle color shifts towards warm or cool tones depending on light. Shallow to medium depth of field, natural optical imperfections like slight vignetting and gentle softness in corners. Rich, deep blacks and muted, earthy colors with a timeless, nostalgic feel. The image has a lived-in, organic quality, with no digital sharpening or plastic look. Realistic textures of skin, fabric, and surfaces are preserved. Perfect for scenes requiring emotional depth and authenticity.
  Analog Photo = Authentic analog photograph, taken with a 35mm film camera using high-speed film stock. Visible film grain structure, natural color shifts and slight color bleeding typical of analog processes. Soft, slightly imperfect focus with gentle halation around bright light sources. Rich texture in shadows, natural light leaks possible. The image has depth and tactility, reminiscent of vintage documentary photography. Warm analog color palette, subtle fade in the blacks, genuine filmic atmosphere. Looks like a real photo from a family album or a photojournalist's contact sheet.
