  Anime 2 = Medium & finish: Digital painting with ethereal, soft-focus finishes—mix of delicate brushwork and smooth gradients that read like watercolor plus light airbrushing. Palette & lighting: Muted, desaturated palettes punctuated by luminous highlights and subtle color accents; frequent cool tones (blues, grays) with warm focal glows. Rendering & detail: highly‑realistic anime to painterly rendering—finely detailed faces and hands, looser treatment of hair, fabrics, and background; delicate texture on skin and cloth. Techniques & hallmarks: Soft rim and backlighting, flowing hair and fabric motion, cinematic depth with fog/particle effects.
  Anime 3 = DGS (Dynamic Game Studio) anime style. Overall look: Clean, modern anime aesthetic blending sharp linework with soft painterly shading; polished commercial‑anime finish. Character design: Slim, stylized proportions; expressive, large eyes with detailed irises; distinct silhouette and costume motifs per character for instant recognition. Linework & color: Crisp, consistent outlines paired with flat base colors and layered cel‑plus‑soft shading; selective highlights on hair and eyes. Lighting & rendering: Mix of cel shading for clothing and harder edges with subtle gradients and bloom for skin and hair — cinematic yet readable.
  Anime 4 = Bold, polished anime-inspired digital illustration with a contemporary game/animation finish. Linework: crisp, clean outlines with confident contour lines; line weight is controlled and often thin, letting color and shape define form more than heavy inking. Color palette: saturated, high-contrast colors with neon-adjacent accents (bright blues, yellows, reds) set against cleaner midtones; deliberate rim/edge highlights in contrasting hues add punch. Rendering & shading: hard cel-shading with selective soft gradients — strong two- or three-tone shadows define muscles and clothing folds; specular highlights are used sparingly to emphasize volume and glossy surfaces. Hair & facial features: angular, dynamic hair shapes with simplified facial features typical of modern anime (large expressive eyes, small noses). Costume design: graphic, costume-forward detailing with clear silhouettes and readable shapes; use of contrasting trim and accents guides the eye. Edge treatment & effects: colored outlines and slight chromatic-offset glow (thin cyan/magenta fringes) give a print/postcard or modern-cel look and increase visual energy. Overall influence: contemporary JRPG/ fighting-game character art mixed with anime character-poster design — sleek, high-energy, and character-driven.
